t rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Eugene Vindman (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Eugene Vindman, a first-term Democratic incumbent, seeks re-election in a Virginia district that leans Democratic by about two points. He has raised more than $12 million and holds roughly $6.6 million on hand, while Republican Doug Ollivant has raised about $250,000. Ollivant announced in early October that he has blood cancer but says he will stay in the race. Minor-party and independent candidates trail far behind.\n\nExpert raters broadly place the race in the Safe or Likely Democratic column, and prediction markets give Vindman roughly a 94 to 95 percent chance of winning. With no public general-election polling, the forecast rests on fundamentals, money, and ratings, all of which point to a comfortable Vindman win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.972, "margin": 13.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9562, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9406, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9612, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9637, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9667, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9827, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9791, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9746, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9559, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9685, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9681, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9696, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9686, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9744, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9771, "margin": 13.0}]}